   "text": {
    "L1": "A roti begins with grains, not at the shop.",
    "L2": "Farmers sow seeds, water them and help the crop grow.",
    "L3": "When the crop is ripe, it is harvested. Threshing separates grains from stalks.",
    "L4": "Winnowing uses wind to blow away the light husk, leaving cleaner grain.",
    "L5": "The grains go to a chakki or mill, where they are ground into atta.",
    "L6": "Atta is cooked into roti. Many people, plus water, land, time and fuel, help along the way.",
    "L7": "So take only what you can eat, store food properly and use safe leftovers. Spoiled food must not be eaten.",
    "L8": "Now put the main steps in order."
   },
